<h1>k-connected graph</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="connectedGraph.html"><em>connected graph</em></a> such that deleting any k-1 <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertices</em></a> (and incident <a href="edge.html"><em>edges</em></a>) results in a graph that is still connected.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="biconnectedGraph.html"><em>biconnected graph</em></a>, <a href="triconnectedGraph.html"><em>triconnected graph</em></a>, <a href="cutvertex.html"><em>cut vertex</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Informally, there are at least k independent <a href="path.html"><em>paths</em></a> from any vertex to any other vertex.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPMS">PMS</a></p>

